{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id351261967"}, "name":{"label":"Elongated muskrat 69"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-11-19T03:32:54-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"10.10.0"}, "id":{"label":"14808301275"}, "title":{"label":"Annoying and not worth the money"}, "content":{"label":"Honestly, even the free version is not worth it when it comes to period tracking.  I could and now do literally track my own cycle.  This is because the UI bombards you with notifications and ads about getting a paid subscription.\n\nWhen I first got the app, I was under the impression that you needed to pay to get access to any features- but the main difference I noticed was these surveys that basically prompted you and fear mongered you into doing a 15-20 min survey that didn’t really tell you anything useful.  \n\nSometimes it was actively unhelpful.  E.g. any time I listed any symptom it would tell me that it could be PCOS, and that I should get it checked out immediately.  Literally even just headaches and cramps.  So I dropped a ton of money on an ultrasound and was told by my GP to never listen to period tracking apps like Flo.  \n\nIn my view, some of these engagement tactics are quite predatory for a women’s help app.  If I could give 0 stars I would.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1038369065&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
